# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DevCatToolRegistry import tool ignores
#
# This is a Node/npm workspace (backend) plus Unity Editor sources (front end).
# It is NOT a Unity project: there is no Assets/ or ProjectSettings/ here, so
# Unity's generated directories only appear if someone opens it as one by mistake.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- OS noise ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- Node -------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- editor / IDE state -----------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs

# --- .NET / Unity build output ---------------------------------------------
# obj/ and Library/ are always build output, so a bare rule is safe for them.
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.dll

# *.csproj is NOT ignored wholesale, for the same reason [Bb]in/ is not: the
# type-check harness IS a .csproj, and a bare rule here silently excluded it from
# every commit. A fresh clone then had only UnityStubs.cs, so `npm run check:csharp`
# died with MSBUILD error MSB1003 ("no project or solution file") -- and the runner
# printed "the errors above are in the real front-end sources", which pointed at
# innocent code. Generated projects are ignored by location instead.
frontends/**/*.csproj
**/Library/*.csproj
*.sln

# bin/ is NOT ignored wholesale: this repository has a source directory called
# apps/cli/bin/, and an unanchored [Bb]in/ rule silently excluded the CLI's entry
# point from every commit. A fresh clone therefore had no `utool` at all, which is
# exactly the failure a repository migration would expose. Only build output named
# bin/ is ignored, and only where it is generated.
tools/csharp-check/bin/
tools/csharp-check/obj/
frontends/**/bin/
frontends/**/obj/

# --- scratch ----------------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
*.local.json
*.local.md
# one-off probes written while debugging; never part of the tool
probe-*.mjs
probe-*.js

# --- release artifacts -------------------------------------------------------
# Built by tools/make-release.mjs from a tag; never committed.
dist/

# --- csharp-check scratch -----------------------------------------------------
# The harness copies the front-end sources here before compiling them; it is an
# output directory, so a bare generated/ would be safe as well, but it is spelled
# out to keep the next reader from having to check.
tools/csharp-check/generated/
